{
  "title": "oRings FX",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Idea",
      "lines": [
        "The incoming audio",
        "strikes a resonator:",
        "a modal body or",
        "strings ring at",
        "FREQ and decay on",
        "their own. The DSP",
        "is the original",
        "open-source Rings",
        "code, run at 48 kHz."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Main page",
      "lines": [
        "MIX: dry <-> wet.",
        "0% = input as is.",
        "STRUCT: partials /",
        "string spacing.",
        "BRIGHT: excitation",
        "brightness.",
        "DAMP: ring length.",
        "POS: where it is",
        "struck (timbre).",
        "FREQ: resonator",
        "note, C0..C7.",
        "MODEL: see Models.",
        "LEVEL: wet level."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Models",
      "lines": [
        "MODAL: plates, bars,",
        "bells. Hats ->",
        "bell tones.",
        "SYMPA: sympathetic",
        "strings.",
        "STRNG: inharmonic,",
        "modulated string.",
        "KVERB: Karplusverb.",
        "FM: 2-op FM, input",
        "envelope drives it.",
        "CHORD: Western",
        "Chords.",
        "DP-*: Disastrous",
        "Peace. The input",
        "goes through its",
        "effect; hits strum",
        "the chord machine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Strum",
      "lines": [
        "A strum moves the",
        "input to the next",
        "voice and fires the",
        "internal exciter.",
        "AUTO: Rings' own",
        "onset detector",
        "(needs ~1 s to",
        "settle).",
        "MIDI: note-on =",
        "strum.",
        "OFF: never. The",
        "input still rings",
        "the resonator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Advanced page",
      "lines": [
        "IN GN: input level",
        "into Rings.",
        "SENS: onset",
        "sensitivity (AUTO).",
        "EXCITE: Rings' own",
        "pluck/strike on",
        "each strum, on top",
        "of the input.",
        "POLY: 1/2/4 voices.",
        "ROUTE: STEREO, ODD",
        "or EVEN only.",
        "FINE: +-100 cents.",
        "WIDTH: 0 = mono sum",
        "-- = no effect now."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Latency",
      "lines": [
        "Wet path: 72 samp.",
        "(1.6 ms). The dry",
        "path is delayed the",
        "same, so the two",
        "line up in the MIX."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
